Here’s a clean, complete, and easy‑to‑understand explanation of Pagination in MuleSoft — how it works, its types, and examples for APIs and databases.

✅ What is Pagination in MuleSoft?
Pagination means retrieving data in small chunks (pages) instead of loading everything at once.

In MuleSoft, pagination is used when:

Calling an external API that returns paginated data
Reading large datasets from a database
Integrating with Salesforce, SAP, GitHub, Jira, etc.
Avoiding memory overload or performance issues
✅ Why Pagination Is Needed?
✅ Improves performance
✅ Avoids timeouts
✅ Avoids “Out of Memory” errors
✅ Reduces load on external systems
✅ Helps integrate with APIs that require page/limit parameters

✅ Types of Pagination in MuleSoft
MuleSoft commonly deals with three pagination patterns:

✅ 1. Offset‑Based Pagination
Typical for REST APIs, SQL databases.

Example:

?page=1&limit=50
?page=2&limit=50
✅ MuleSoft Example:



XML
<http:request path="users" method="GET">
    <http:query-params><![CDATA[
        {
            "page": vars.page,
            "limit": 50
        }
    ]]></http:query-params>
</http:request>
Loop until no records returned.

✅ 2. Cursor / Token‑Based Pagination
Used by Salesforce, Jira, GitHub.

Example:

nextPageToken = "a8x9f...."
Each response gives next cursor, Mule continues until cursor is null.

✅ MuleSoft Flow:
Call API → Extract nextToken → Repeat until token = null
✅ 3. Time‑Based Pagination
Used in logs, audit APIs.

Example:

?startTime=2024-01-01&endTime=2024-01-02
Mule moves window by time slices.

✅ Pagination with Database Connector (Streaming)
When reading large DB data, MuleSoft uses streaming + paging:




XML
<db:select fetchSize="200">
    <db:sql>SELECT * FROM EMPLOYEES</db:sql>
</db:select>
✅ fetchSize controls how many rows Mule loads per batch.

✅ Pagination Using Scatter‑Gather / Until Successful
Most Mule flows use While or Repeatable loops:




XML
<while expression="#[vars.hasNextPage]">
    <flow-ref name="GetNextPage"/>
</while>
✅ MuleSoft Pagination Example – API Pagination Loop
Step 1: Initialize



XML
<set-variable name="page" value="1"/>
<set-variable name="hasNext" value="true"/>
Step 2: Loop



XML
<while expression="#[vars.hasNext]">
    <flow-ref name="CallAPI"/>
    <set-variable name="page" value="#[vars.page + 1]"/>
</while>
Step 3: Stop when records < limit



XML
<choice>
    <when expression="#[sizeOf(payload.data) < 50]">
        <set-variable name="hasNext" value="false"/>
    </when>
</choice>
✅ Pagination in MuleSoft + Salesforce Connector
Salesforce uses QueryMore to retrieve next batch (2000 rows per chunk):




XML
<salesforce:query query="SELECT Id, Name FROM Account"/>
<salesforce:queryMore/>
