✅ What Is Streaming in MuleSoft?
Streaming in MuleSoft allows processing large data (files, database results, HTTP payloads) without loading the entire content into memory.

Instead of reading everything at once, Mule processes the data as a stream in chunks, which avoids memory overload and improves performance.

✅ Why Streaming Is Important?
✅ Prevents Out‑Of‑Memory errors
✅ Handles large payloads like CSV, XML, JSON
✅ Improves performance & scalability
✅ Supports real‑time transformation of large datasets
✅ Efficient memory usage

✅ Where MuleSoft Uses Streaming?
Mule automatically enables streaming for:
Database Connector (DB streaming)
File Connector (large file reading)
HTTP Listener & HTTP Request (streaming mode)
Transform Message (DataWeave supports streaming)
✅ Types of Streaming in MuleSoft
MuleSoft supports three major types:

✅ 1. Non‑Repeatable Stream
Stream can be read only once
If you try to read again → error
Used when:

Payload is too large to buffer in memory
Reading input stream directly from HTTP
✅ 2. Repeatable In-Memory Stream
Small payload stored in memory
Can be re-read (repeatable)
Fast but limited by RAM
✅ Works for payloads < ~1MB (default threshold)

✅ 3. Repeatable File Store Stream
Large streams cached on the file system
Good for huge payloads (CSV, XLSX, XML)
✅ Safer than in-memory
✅ Prevents OOM errors

✅ How to Enable Streaming in Mule 4?
✅ Streaming in HTTP Request Connector



XML
<http:request streaming="ALWAYS">
Modes:

ALWAYS
AUTO (default)
NEVER
✅ DB Streaming Example
Database connector automatically streams rows instead of loading everything at once.




XML
<db:select fetchSize="200">
    <db:sql>SELECT * FROM EMPLOYEES</db:sql>
</db:select>
✅ fetchSize controls how many rows are streamed per batch.

✅ File Streaming Example



XML
<file:read path="large.csv" streaming="true"/>
Mule reads file chunk-by-chunk, not entire file.

